<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NK">Construction <span data-tag="04NK">9.6.4.17</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a lifting problem </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  X \ar [d] \\ B \ar [r] \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur] &amp;  Y. } \]
</div>
<p> in an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, given by a morphism $\sigma : \Delta ^1 \times \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. We let $\operatorname{Sol}( \sigma )$ denote the simplicial set $ \{  \sigma \}  \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}( Q, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^3, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, where $Q \subset \Delta ^3$ is the simplicial subset described in Remark <a data-tag="04ML" href="/tag/04ML">9.6.4.2</a>. We will refer to $\operatorname{Sol}( \sigma )$ as the <em>space of solutions</em> to the lifting problem $\sigma $. </p>
